cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  qntt: quantum-number-preserving block-sparse tensor trains
  for fermionic many-body systems
message: >-
  If qntt contributes to work you publish, please cite it using the metadata below.
  A methods paper is in preparation and will replace this software citation as the
  preferred reference once it appears.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cazeaux
    given-names: Paul
    email: cazeaux@vt.edu
    affiliation: Virginia Tech
abstract: >-
  qntt implements matrix-product-state / tensor-train methods for electronic structure
  and fermionic lattice problems. Spin-up and spin-down electron counts, or on the
  spin-adapted layer the total spin, are held exactly as block-sparse quantum numbers on
  every tensor core rather than enforced by penalty or recovered by projection.
  The library provides two symmetry layers (abelian Nup/Ndn-conserving and SU(2)
  spin-adapted), abelian point-group symmetry on both, an ALS/MALS/TDVP/Riemannian solver
  stack, excited states, and linear response (RPA/TDA) including joint orbital-TT response,
  with a C ABI and Julia bindings.
version: 0.1.1
date-released: '2026-11-12'
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: https://github.com/paulcazeaux/QNTensorTrains-rs
keywords:
  - tensor train
  - matrix product state
  - DMRG
  - electronic structure
  - quantum chemistry
  - spin adaptation
  - SU(2) symmetry
  - point-group symmetry
  - Rust
# The concept DOI: it resolves to the latest archived version.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24167856
